ittle, but this script has been in      use on my machine for a while, to check the current ToT      firmware version numbers, or see what hardware we have      firmware for on a given platform, or get a direct path to      an ebuild file.  It has worked so far. BUG=None  Change-Id: I30964b065462fab16fd2c6bf519dfc0dea778ada Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334393 Commit-Ready: Katherine Threlkeld &lt;kathrelkeld@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Katherine Threlkeld &lt;kathrelkeld@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334393" owner_email="kathrelkeld@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/crostestutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crostestutils" ref="refs/changes/93/334393/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I11198b0b675056a1f168662d89666d8919b3bc85" commit="9d7ed2bf93babe0f04d53ce4dbf0caf9112d9e8b" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Revert &quot;epoll: use freezable blocking call&quot;  This reverts commit 067c9aa915378b4c26799ab5240051b9bdf4339b. We're having issues in the field with segfaults inside libevent and this has caused memory corruption in the past.  BUG=chromium:596124 TEST=make  Change-Id: I11198b0b675056a1f168662d89666d8919b3bc85 Signed-off-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334454 Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334454" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/54/334454/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If3d492f0d4e2dcbd62f2f7c8dd9f25c590a3db84"